  "prompt": "Are doctors' professional fees subject to VAT?",
  "runtimeCommit": "87ce0c7571f9bd57514b6c2dfb45e9427d19c6b6",
  "answer": "### Issue Presented\nAre doctors' professional fees subject to Value-Added Tax (VAT)?\n\n### Short Answer\nDoctors' professional fees are generally subject to VAT unless specifically exempted under the National Internal Revenue Code (NIRC).\n\n### Legal Interpretation\n\n### Practical Application\nIn practice, doctors who are VAT-registered must charge VAT on their professional fees. They should ensure that their billing reflects the VAT component and comply with the necessary documentation requirements for VAT purposes. However, if a doctor qualifies for any specific exemptions under the law, they may not be required to charge VAT. It is advisable for medical practitioners to consult with a tax professional to determine their specific VAT obligations based on their services and clientele.",
